@page "/privacy"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<h1 class="display-4">Privacy</h1>
<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
    This is a development sample, not a production privacy policy. Replace this page with your application's policy before deployment.
</div>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h5 card-title">Information used by the sample</h2>
        <p>The sample requests only the <code>atproto</code> identity scope. It displays your DID, access token expiration and client signing key ID.
            It does not request profile or timeline permissions.</p>
        <p>Authentication credentials and login correlation state are held in memory. Authentication and correlation cookies support login,
            and additional cookies protect forms against forgery and carry the refresh status message.</p>
        <p>Logging out removes the local session and attempts to revoke its tokens. Restarting the sample clears its in-memory sessions.</p>
        <p class="mb-0">The hosting environment, tunnel provider and authorization server may process request and diagnostic information.
            Review their settings and policies when configuring your own deployment.</p>
    </div>
</div>
